<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait credit extension up 2.5 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Kuwait credit extension up 2.5 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic credit extended by Kuwaiti banks rose 2.5 percent to 2.740 billion dinars at the end of June from 2.672 billion at the end of May, Central Bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The credit amounted to 2.113 billion dinars at the end of June 1995. Balance of cash portion used from domestic credit facilities by sector:</p>
<p>			 Figures in million dinars</p>
<p>					  June '96	    June '95</p>
<p>Trade				     454.0		  635.4</p>
<p>Industry				  232.8		  143.7</p>
<p>Construction			    178.5		  133.8</p>
<p>Agriculture and Fishing		 9.7		    7.7</p>
<p>Non-bank financial</p>
<p> institutions			   128.4		  139.8</p>
<p>Personal Facilities		  1273.9		  591.1</p>
<p>Real Estate			     301.7		  293.9</p>
<p>Other				     161.8		  167.4</p>
<p>Total				    2740.7		 2112.8</p>
<p> of which, consumer loans	   517.2		  526.8</p>
<p>Note: Non-bank financial institutions include insurance, money exchange and investment firms. The figures include the effect of purchasing the debts of Kuwaiti debtors in return for Debt Purchase Bonds since December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.2999 dinars.</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom 965 -243-1920</p>
</text>
